What SpringApplication.run() ACTUALLY does
ConfigurableApplicationContext context =
    SpringApplication.run(RemoteSeaProbeApplication.class, args);

Internally it:

Creates the ApplicationContext

Loads auto-configurations

Scans components

Creates beans

Starts embedded Tomcat

Starts background threads

Returns control back to main

✔ Yes, beans exist after this line
❌ But main() is NOT a managed Spring bean
