Q: What is @ConditionalOnSingleCandidate in Spring Boot?
It ensures auto-configuration activates only when exactly one candidate bean of a required type exists.
This prevents ambiguity, especially in cases like multiple DataSources,
where Spring Boot refuses to guess and disables auto-config unless a primary is defined.
---------------------
@ConfigurationProperties  → config binding
@ConditionalOnClass       → library present?
@ConditionalOnBean        → dependency exists?
@ConditionalOnSingleCandidate → no ambiguity?
---------------------
What it means in plain English

“Enable Hibernate JPA auto-configuration ONLY IF exactly one DataSource bean exists.”

Why?

Because if Spring finds:

0 DataSources → nothing to connect to

2+ DataSources → ambiguity

Spring Boot refuses to guess
